<li><a href="/wiki/Template:PD-Mexico-NIP" title="Template:PD-Mexico-NIP"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{PD-Mexico-NIP}}</span></a> – all information published at <a rel="nofollow" class="external free" href="http://fuente.presidencia.gob.mx/">http://fuente.presidencia.gob.mx/</a> before April 2006.</li>
<li><a href="/wiki/Template:LGACDMX" title="Template:LGACDMX"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{LGACDMX}}</span></a> – all open information published at "cdmx.gob.mx" websites.</li></ul>
<div class="mw-heading mw-heading2 ext-discussiontools-init-section"><h2 id="Currency" data-mw-thread-id="h-Currency"><span data-mw-comment-start="" id="h-Currency"></span>Currency<span data-mw-comment-end="h-Currency"></span></h2></div>
<p><span id="CUR"></span>
</p>
<div class="shortcut2" style="background:var(--background-color-neutral-subtle, #f8f9fa); color:var(--color-base, #202122);" role="note"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r927745239"><a href="/wiki/Commons:Shortcuts" title="Commons:Shortcuts">Shortcut</a><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r574572692"><div class="plainlist">
<ul><li><span class="plainlinks"><a class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:CUR_Mexico&amp;redirect=no" href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:CUR_Mexico&amp;redirect=no">COM:CUR Mexico</a></span></li></ul>
</div></div>
<p><span dir="ltr">See also: <a href="/wiki/Commons:Currency" title="Commons:Currency">Commons:Currency</a></span>
</p><p><span typeof="mw:File"><span><img src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/OOjs_UI_icon_close-ltr-destructive.svg/20px-OOjs_UI_icon_close-ltr-destructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/OOjs_UI_icon_close-ltr-destructive.svg/40px-OOjs_UI_icon_close-ltr-destructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="20" data-file-height="20"></span></span>&nbsp;<b>Not OK</b> Mexican currency is copyrighted and the reproduction of designs is only permitted by seeking authorisation from the Ministry of Finance (Secretaría de Hacienda y Crédito Público).<sup id="cite_ref-9" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-9"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup><sup id="cite_ref-10" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-10"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
Coins and banknotes produced before 23 July 1928 entered the public domain before the law changed on 23 July 2003, and remain in the public domain. 
</p>
<div class="mw-heading mw-heading2 ext-discussiontools-init-section"><h2 id="Freedom_of_panorama" data-mw-thread-id="h-Freedom_of_panorama"><span data-mw-comment-start="" id="h-Freedom_of_panorama"></span>Freedom of panorama<span data-mw-comment-end="h-Freedom_of_panorama"></span></h2></div>
<p><span id="FOP"></span>
</p>
<div class="shortcut2" style="background:var(--background-color-neutral-subtle, #f8f9fa); color:var(--color-base, #202122);" role="note"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r927745239"><a href="/wiki/Commons:Shortcuts" title="Commons:Shortcuts">Shortcut</a><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r574572692"><div class="plainlist">
<ul><li><span class="plainlinks"><a class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:FOP_Mexico&amp;redirect=no" href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:FOP_Mexico&amp;redirect=no">COM:FOP Mexico</a></span></li></ul>
</div></div>
<p><span dir="ltr">See also: <a href="/wiki/Commons:Freedom_of_panorama" title="Commons:Freedom of panorama">Commons:Freedom of panorama</a></span>
</p><p><span typeof="mw:File"><span><img src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg/20px-OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg/40px-OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="20" data-file-height="20"></span></span> <b>OK</b> {{<a href="/wiki/Template:FoP-Mexico" title="Template:FoP-Mexico">FoP-Mexico</a>}} 
</p><p>Mexico's copyright law allows the reproduction of copyrighted works without compensation under certain circumstances, one of them being works that are visible from public places:
</p>
<dl><dd><i>Literary and artistic works that have already been disclosed may only be used in the following cases without the consent of the owner of the economic rights and without remuneration, provided that the normal exploitation of the work is not adversely affected thereby and provided also that the source is invariably mentioned and that no alteration is made to the work: [...]</i>
<ul><li><i>Reproduction, communication and distribution by means of drawings, paintings, photographs and audiovisual processes of works that are visible from public places."</i><span style="color:gray;font-size:80%;"><sup>[1996-2018 Art.148(VII)]</sup></span></li></ul></dd></dl>
<p>The term <i>public places</i> has been interpreted to include both indoor and outdoor places that are open to the public. There is no legal secondary approved laws on the exact scope of the term.
</p><p>Independent of copyright law, the (government-owned) Mexico City Metro invokes its administrative authority to require permits for filming and photography inside its facilities.<sup id="cite_ref-11" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-11"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>The Mexican Federal Law on Telecommunications and Broadcasting also uses the term <i>public places</i>. It defines public places as: "...those that are in the charge of dependencies of federal, state or municipal entities, or under public programs of any one of the three orders of government..." Under this law, public places include:
</p>
<ul><li>schools, universities, and every kind of building used for education;</li>
<li>clinics, hospitals, and every kind of building used for health care;</li>
<li>government offices of all types;</li>
<li>community centers;</li>
<li>places that are open to the public with free admission such as parks, green areas, and sports centers;</li>
<li>places that collaborate in public federal programs.</li></ul>
<p>However, there is no source claiming that the term <i>public places</i> under Mexican copyright law can be interpreted in the same way.
</p>
<div class="mw-heading mw-heading2 ext-discussiontools-init-section"><h2 id="Threshold_of_originality" data-mw-thread-id="h-Threshold_of_originality"><span data-mw-comment-start="" id="h-Threshold_of_originality"></span>Threshold of originality<span data-mw-comment-end="h-Threshold_of_originality"></span></h2></div>
<p><span id="TOO"></span>
</p>
<div class="shortcut2" style="background:var(--background-color-neutral-subtle, #f8f9fa); color:var(--color-base, #202122);" role="note"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r927745239"><a href="/wiki/Commons:Shortcuts" title="Commons:Shortcuts">Shortcut</a><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r574572692"><div class="plainlist">
<ul><li><span class="plainlinks"><a class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:TOO_Mexico&amp;redirect=no" href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:TOO_Mexico&amp;redirect=no">COM:TOO Mexico</a></span></li></ul>
</div></div>
<p><span dir="ltr">See also: <a href="/wiki/Commons:Threshold_of_originality" title="Commons:Threshold of originality">Commons:Threshold of originality</a></span>
</p><p>As indicated above, the following are examples of what is and what is not protected under the 1996 copyright law:
</p><p>These images are <span typeof="mw:File"><span><img src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg/20px-OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg/40px-OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="20" data-file-height="20"></span></span> <b>OK</b> to upload to Commons
</p>
<ul class="gallery mw-gallery-traditional">
		<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 155px">
			<div class="thumb" style="width: 150px; height: 150px;"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:A%2B_2021.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="Letters, digits or isolated colors"><img alt="Letters, digits or isolated colors" src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/A%2B_2021.svg/120px-A%2B_2021.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="120" height="78" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/A%2B_2021.svg/250px-A%2B_2021.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="497" data-file-height="321"></a></span></div>
			<div class="gallerytext">Letters, digits or isolated colors</div>
		</li>
		<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 155px">
			<div class="thumb" style="width: 150px; height: 150px;"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Museo_National_de_Arte_Mexico_logo.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="Names and titles or isolated phrases"><img alt="Names and titles or isolated phrases" src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Museo_National_de_Arte_Mexico_logo.svg/120px-Museo_National_de_Arte_Mexico_logo.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="120" height="8" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Museo_National_de_Arte_Mexico_logo.svg/250px-Museo_National_de_Arte_Mexico_logo.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="245" data-file-height="17"></a></span></div>
			<div class="gallerytext">Names and titles or isolated phrases</div>
		</li>
		<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 155px">
			<div class="thumb" style="width: 150px; height: 150px;"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Blank_military_form,_1861-1863.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="Simple formats or blank forms to be filled with any type of information, as well as their instructions (example picture)"><img alt="Simple formats or blank forms to be filled with any type of information, as well as their instructions (example picture)" src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Blank_military_form%2C_1861-1863.jpg/120px-Blank_military_form%2C_1861-1863.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="92" height="120" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Blank_military_form%2C_1861-1863.jpg/250px-Blank_military_form%2C_1861-1863.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="10400" data-file-height="13616"></a></span></div>
			<div class="gallerytext">Simple formats or blank forms to be filled with any type of information, as well as their instructions (example picture)</div>
		</li>
		<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 155px">
			<div class="thumb" style="width: 150px; height: 150px;"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Escudo_de_oaxaca.png" class="mw-file-description" title="Reproductions or imitations, without authorization, of shields, flags or emblems of any country, state, municipality or equivalent political division"><img alt="Reproductions or imitations, without authorization, of shields, flags or emblems of any country, state, municipality or equivalent political division" src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Escudo_de_oaxaca.png/120px-Escudo_de_oaxaca.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="120" height="92" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e9/Escudo_de_oaxaca.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x" data-file-width="248" data-file-height="191"></a></span></div>
			<div class="gallerytext">Reproductions or imitations, without authorization, of shields, flags or emblems of any country, state, municipality or equivalent political division</div>
		</li>
		<li class="gallerybox" style="width: 155px">
			<div class="thumb" style="width: 150px; height: 150px;"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Movimiento_Ciudadano.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="Reproductions or imitations, without authorization, of international governmental, non-governmental organizations, or of any other officially recognized organization"><img alt="Reproductions or imitations, without authorization, of international governmental, non-governmental organizations, or of any other officially recognized organization" src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Movimiento_Ciudadano.svg/120px-Movimiento_Ciudadano.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="120" height="80" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Movimiento_Ciudadano.svg/250px-Movimiento_Ciudadano.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1600" data-file-height="1066"></a></span></div>
			<div class="gallerytext">Reproductions or imitations, without authorization, of international governmental, non-governmental organizations, or of any other officially recognized organization</div>
		</li>
</ul>
<p>These are <span typeof="mw:File"><span><img src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/OOjs_UI_icon_close-ltr-destructive.svg/20px-OOjs_UI_icon_close-ltr-destructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/OOjs_UI_icon_close-ltr-destructive.svg/40px-OOjs_UI_icon_close-ltr-destructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="20" data-file-height="20"></span></span>&nbsp;<b>Not OK</b> to upload to Commons (unless published under a free license by the copyright holder), because they are above the threshold of originality required for copyright protection and are not covered by the law itself.
</p>
<div class="mw-heading mw-heading2 ext-discussiontools-init-section"><h2 id="AI-created_works" data-mw-thread-id="h-AI-created_works"><span data-mw-comment-start="" id="h-AI-created_works"></span>AI-created works<span data-mw-comment-end="h-AI-created_works"></span></h2></div>
<p>In Mexico, works exclusively created with artificial intelligence (AI) shall not receive copyright protections as these are linked to human creativity.<sup id="cite_ref-AI_12-0" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-AI-12"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
